The Fast and Furious films have always  been made for a large audience and are  fairly easy to watch all the more reason  for the first of the new Hobson show  some time ago because the scene in which  Luke Hobbs fights his opponents eye out  was too much for the producers instead  the first spin of his aimed at a Peggy  13 age rating in the USA not the  surprise at first but director david  leitch also announced that he has cut  out the tough scenes for the cinema  version yet wants to save them for home  cinema Jason Statham also talks about  the censorship which has caused some  brutal scenes to be cut out in detail he  even talks about the fact that a lot of  things were too x-rated for the movie  which is the highest age rating in the  USA that hasn't been given since 1990  however for fans of the more brutal  entertainment it is likely that these  scenes can be seen on blu-ray at the  latest but before that there will be a  cinema released on August 2nd which  means that we will have to wait a bit  longer for the DVD release the release  of it too is slowly but surely getting  closer in the course of the last weeks  two trailers were released which the  majority of the fans liked very much now  also three pictures have been posted in  advance in a recently published  interview with Collider director Andy  muschietti reveals more details about  the second part of the new edition of it  in the second part the evil clown is  supposed to become even more perverted  and pushed the south proclaim losers  club to its limits with his psycho games  it's no surprise that Pennywise is  supposed to get even worse in the second  part after all he had 27 years to  prepare for his return on the other hand  there are also the meanwhile grown-up  protagonists bill Beverly Ben Ritchie  Eddie and Mike who are determined to  destroy Pennywise perfidious plan a nice  additional info is that it is actually a  she and like in the books she might  produce offspring it will be exciting to  see if the losers Club can defeat it or  if they will literally lose it chapter 2  will be released in cinemas on september  6 2019 soon so the west coast alone will  be back on the screen with his cult  figure John Rambo in the fifth part of  the franchise in an interview last week  he also talked about another popular  film in which he placed the leading role  key this comes as a bit of a surprise as  the 73 year-old salon has repeatedly  announced in the past that he actually  wanted to leave the character Rocky  Balboa behind him now he seems to have  changed his mind as he announced that he  is already working on the script of the  seventh rocky movie similar to Rocky v  the plot will be a bit different from  its predecessors as in the seventh part  Rocky will have to deal with the young  illegal immigrant who is stuck in the  USA the bottom line is that this sounds  very political and salon himself also  thinks that the film will be very  up-to-date unfortunately a release date  isn't fixed yet 35 years after his first  indie action hit Mad Max with Mel Gibson  director George Miller gave his original  film a successor in 2015 the project  which costs about 150 million US dollars  earned about 380 million u.s. dollars  worldwide at the box office and is also  considered by critics to be a successful  action firework at that time Miller also  announced his own Mad Max trilogy with  Tom Hardy but not much has happened  since then in a recently published  interview with indieWIRE Miller explains  that they are just about to solve the  problems of the failed production  however it's pretty clear that a new  movie is coming and it is looking  extremely positive he hasn't said  anything about the more precise date yet  so we'll have to wait a little longer  until we hear more about the sequel of  Mad Max some time ago Andrew Lincoln's  exit from The Walking Dead series caused  a stir they said he wanted to spend more  time with his family but the few days  ago it turned out that Lincoln is  supposed to return as a serial character  Rick Grimes however not in the new  season but at least in his own solo  movie to be seen on the Twitter channel  of AMC at Comic Con though it was mainly  the tenth season and last the film that  played a role which is why a new  announcement about the Walking Dead solo  movie with Rick Grimes is probably not  to be expected at the moment for some  time now cult director Quentin Tarantino  has been talking about retiring after 10  film projects anyone who believes in a  PR gag or something similar is probably  wrong since Tarantino repeated over and  over in past interviews that after 10  movies it would definitely be time to  end only the director's chair of a new  Star Trek film  for him apart from that he really  retires after 10 films number 9 on his  list once upon a time in Hollywood is  about to be released but we do not know  exactly what happens next the script by  Star Trek supposedly already exists but  Tarantino is on the other hand also  interested in Kill Bill 3 we have no  choice but to wait and see when  Tarantino will talk about his new and  last movie four years ago wind Easler  nouns the plan TV series about Riddick  since then nothing has happened a little  surprisingly when diesel now announced  on Instagram that there would be a  Riddick for furia on Instagram he  published the video in which he proudly  holds the script for the new Riddick  film completed by David Bowie in the  camera however it is still uncertain  when the shooting will begin  [Music]
 

